@startuml uc-phy-05-activity
title UC-PHY-05 – Activity diagram (main flow + 2a, 2b)\nC7 sescam-diagnostics v1.0.0
skinparam shadowing false

|Physician (client)|
start
note right
  Preconditions: physician authenticated (SSO);
  procedure ordered (UC-PHY-01) and booked into a slot (UC-AAD-05).
end note
|Server|
:List procedures awaiting execution\n(booked orders without an execution record);
|Physician (client)|
:1. Select the active or recently completed procedure;
:2. Enter execution details: actual start and end,\nroom/equipment, contrast batch and volume,\nradiation dose (DLP, CTDIvol), radiotracer activity,\ninformed consent verified;
if (2a. Clinical or operational incident?) then (yes)
  :Document incident: type, severity\n(mild / moderate / severe), narrative,\ntreatment given;
  if (2b. Incident prevents completing\nthe examination?) then (yes)
    :Mark procedure as aborted, give reason;
  else (no)
  endif
else (no)
endif
:Validate form (mandatory fields, end after start);
:3. Submit execution log;

|Server|
if (Actor may log executions\n(physician / radiologist / technician)?) then (no)
  :Audit EXECUTION_ACCESS_DENIED;
  |Physician (client)|
  :Show "not authorized";
  stop
else (yes)
endif
|Server|
if (Procedure exists and awaits execution?) then (no)
  |Physician (client)|
  :Show "procedure not found"\nor "already recorded";
  stop
else (yes)
endif
|Server|
if (Data valid? (times, consent verified when required,\ncontrast batch with contrast, dose fields\nrequired by the modality, aborted => incident)) then (no)
  |Physician (client)|
  :Show invalid fields; nothing stored;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
|Server|
if (2b. Aborted?) then (yes)
  :Persist execution with status INCOMPLETE_INCIDENT\nand its incidents (linked to the patient);
  :Audit PROCEDURE_ABORTED and CLINICAL_INCIDENT_LOGGED;
  :Publish ProcedureExecutionEvent(INCOMPLETE_INCIDENT)\nfor Admissions rescheduling and Orders status;
  |Physician (client)|
  :Show "Procedure aborted. Admissions notified for rescheduling";
  stop
else (no)
  |Server|
  :4. Persist execution with status EXECUTED_PENDING_REPORT\n(+ incidents of 2a, linked to the patient);
  :Audit EXECUTION_RECORDED\n(+ CLINICAL_INCIDENT_LOGGED per incident);
  :Publish ProcedureExecutionEvent(EXECUTED_PENDING_REPORT)\nfor Orders status;
  |Physician (client)|
  :5. Confirm execution recording;
  stop
endif
@enduml
